.TH @NAME_UPPER@ 1 "" "@DISPLAY_NAME@ @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@NAME@ \- terminal emulator with syntax highlighting for network devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @NAME@
.RB [ \-d
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR CONFIG ]
.RB [ \-T
.IR TITLE ]
.RB [ \-\-class
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-hold ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR command " [" args ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @DISPLAY_NAME@
is a GPU-rendered terminal emulator for Wayland and X11. It has tabs, split
panes, themes, true transparency, inline images (sixel and kitty graphics), the
kitty keyboard protocol and desktop notifications.
.PP
Output from Cisco, Arista and Juniper devices is highlighted with PCRE2 rules
read from
.I .ini
profiles. The profile is chosen automatically from what appears on screen.
.PP
A sidebar holds saved SSH, Telnet, serial and local sessions in folders, and a
file explorer that browses the focused SSH session's server over SFTP (or SCP
when the device has no SFTP).
.PP
Clicking in the line you are typing moves the cursor there.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exec " \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]"
Run
.I command
instead of the login shell. This must be the last option; everything after it
is passed to the command.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-directory " \fIDIR\fR"
Start in
.IR DIR .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Read
.I FILE
instead of
.IR ~/.config/@NAME@/config.ini .
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-title " \fITITLE\fR"
Set the initial window title.
.TP
.BI \-\-class " ID"
Set the application id (Wayland) or WM_CLASS (X11). The default is
.BR @APP_ID@ .
.TP
.B \-\-hold
Keep panes open after their command exits.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print debug logging to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH KEYS
These are the defaults. Every shortcut can be changed in the
.B [keys]
section of
.IR config.ini .
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C, Ctrl+Shift+V
Copy the selection, paste the clipboard.
.TP
.B Shift+Insert, middle click
Paste the primary selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+F
Search the scrollback (regex).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+T, Ctrl+Shift+W
New tab, close pane.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+E, Ctrl+Shift+O
Split right, split down.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+H
Cycle highlighting: auto, off, then each profile.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+R
Reload the configuration (also automatic when files change).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+.
Switch to the next installed theme.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+B
Show or hide the sidebar.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
Quick connect (SSH, Telnet or serial without saving).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+=, Ctrl+Shift+-, Ctrl+Shift+0
Zoom in, zoom out, reset.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/@NAME@/config.ini
Main configuration. An annotated example is installed as
.IR @DATADIR@/config.ini.example .
.TP
.I ~/.config/@NAME@/themes/
Your own themes. Bundled themes are in
.IR @DATADIR@/themes/ .
.TP
.I ~/.config/@NAME@/highlight/
Your own highlighting profiles. A file with the same profile name as a bundled
one in
.I @DATADIR@/highlight/
replaces it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/@NAME@/sessions/
Saved sessions, one
.I .ini
file per session (mode 0600). Passwords are never stored.
.PP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is used instead of
.I ~/.config
when it is set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Programs started in the terminal see
.BR TERM=xterm-256color ,
.B COLORTERM=truecolor
and
.BR TERM_PROGRAM=@DISPLAY_NAME@ .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sftp (1),
.BR scp (1)
.SH AUTHOR
@AUTHOR@ <@EMAIL@>
